[E0427] Error: a field cannot hold `&(i64) => i64`
   ╭─[ err/103_closures/main.wip:9:8 ]
   │
 9 │     f: &(x: i64) => i64             // a field cannot hold a reference
   │        ────────┬───────  
   │                ╰───────── `&(i64) => i64` borrows, as a `str` does
   │ 
   │ Help: write `view struct`, for a struct that borrows
   │ 
   │ Note: a `str`, a `&` reference, a `view struct` and what holds one borrow what lives somewhere else, so they stand in a parameter, a local, a result and a view's field, and not where they would outlive it
───╯
[E0304] Error: cannot assign to `total`, which this closure only reads
    ╭─[ err/103_closures/main.wip:19:9 ]
    │
 19 │         total += x
    │         ──┬──  
    │           ╰──── captured to read
    │ 
    │ Help: write the lambda where a `&var (…) => R` is taken, or take what changes as a `&var` parameter of it
    │ 
    │ Note: a closure lent as `&(…) => R`, or kept in a `val`, reads what it captures; one that changes it is a `&var (…) => R`, lent for the call it is written in
────╯
[E0350] Error: a lambda that uses `factor` from around it is a closure
    ╭─[ err/103_closures/main.wip:26:22 ]
    │
 26 │     plain((x) => x * factor, 2)     // a plain function captures nothing
    │                      ───┬──  
    │                         ╰──── captured here
    │ 
    │ Help: take it as a parameter of the lambda, declare the parameter a closure, or keep the lambda in a `val`
    │ 
    │ Note: a plain function value captures nothing; a closure is `&(…) => R` or `&var (…) => R`, lent for one call, or kept in a `val` it is the whole value of, reading what it captures
────╯
